waiver: harness-limit
reason: usize is the target's pointer width, so its wrap point is defined
  per target and a case carries one expected.stdout. This case pins the
  64-bit targets; usize_wraps_at_32_bits pins wasm32 with the same
  operations. The interpreter models its host, which is 64-bit wherever the
  corpus runs; internal/oracle/interp's TestUsizeWrapsAtTheHostPointerWidth
  pins its 32-bit rule.
